@prefix doap: <http://usefulinc.com/ns/doap#> .
@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix lv2: <http://lv2plug.in/ns/lv2core#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix units: <http://lv2plug.in/ns/extensions/units#> .

<http://dataforte.stom-pi#me>
    a foaf:Person ;
    foaf:name "Dataforte" .

<http://dataforte.stom-pi/plugins/eclecticmistress>
    a doap:Project ;
    doap:maintainer <http://dataforte.stom-pi#me> ;
    doap:name "Eclectic Mistress" .

<http://dataforte.stom-pi/plugins/eclecticmistress>
    a lv2:Plugin ,
        lv2:FlangerPlugin ;
    doap:maintainer <http://dataforte.stom-pi#me> ;
    doap:name "Eclectic Mistress" ;
    doap:license <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0> ;
    lv2:project <http://dataforte.stom-pi/plugins/eclecticmistress> ;
    lv2:optionalFeature lv2:hardRTCapable ;

    lv2:minorVersion 1 ;
    lv2:microVersion 0 ;

rdfs:comment """

Faust-based emulation of the Electro-Harmonix Electric Mistress flanger.

The Electric Mistress is a bucket brigade delay (BBD) whose delay time is
swept by an LFO and mixed with the dry signal to form a swept comb filter.
The delayed signal is fed back through the COLOR pot to the input of the
gain stage, giving the iconic resonant "sucked-in" flanging sound.

Implemented signal path (after the 1976 V2 circuit):
    input highpass (300 Hz) -> resonant comb (feedback = COLOR)
    -> dry + delayed sum -> response-restoration lowpass (6 kHz)
    -> mild saturation -> wet/dry mix.

Controls:
    RATE   LFO sweep speed in Hz (0 = fixed delay, "Filter Matrix" mode)
    RANGE  LFO sweep width, % of the full BBD delay range (0.5..5 ms)
    COLOR  feedback amount and polarity, -100%..+100%
            (positive reinforces comb peaks, negative inverts feedback)
    MIX    wet/dry mix, 0..100 %

Reference: R. Metzger, "The Mistress Mystery Page",
http://www.metzgerralf.de/elekt/stomp/mistress/index.shtml

""";

    lv2:port [
        a lv2:InputPort ,
            lv2:ControlPort ;
        lv2:index 0 ;
        lv2:symbol "rate" ;
        lv2:name "RATE";
        lv2:default 0.9 ;
        lv2:minimum 0.0 ;
        lv2:maximum 3.0 ;
        units:unit units:hz ;
    ] , [
        a lv2:InputPort ,
            lv2:ControlPort ;
        lv2:index 1 ;
        lv2:symbol "range" ;
        lv2:name "RANGE";
        lv2:default 30.0 ;
        lv2:minimum 0.0 ;
        lv2:maximum 100.0 ;
    ] , [
        a lv2:InputPort ,
            lv2:ControlPort ;
        lv2:index 2 ;
        lv2:symbol "color" ;
        lv2:name "COLOR";
        lv2:default 30.0 ;
        lv2:minimum -100.0 ;
        lv2:maximum 100.0 ;
    ] , [
        a lv2:InputPort ,
            lv2:ControlPort ;
        lv2:index 3 ;
        lv2:symbol "mix" ;
        lv2:name "MIX";
        lv2:default 100.0 ;
        lv2:minimum 0.0 ;
        lv2:maximum 100.0 ;
    ] , [
        a lv2:AudioPort ,
            lv2:OutputPort ;
        lv2:index 4 ;
        lv2:symbol "out" ;
        lv2:name "Out" ;
    ] , [
        a lv2:AudioPort ,
            lv2:InputPort ;
        lv2:index 5 ;
        lv2:symbol "in" ;
        lv2:name "In" ;
    ] .
